---
source: crates/ry-checker/tests/corpus.rs
expression: rows
---
- case: user mean with a default argument is clean
  diagnostics: []
- case: the mtcars dataset is a known value
  diagnostics: []
- case: subset() resolves a column name inside the data frame
  diagnostics: []
- case: print dispatches to a user S3 method
  diagnostics: []
- case: NA in a double vector keeps arithmetic and mean() well typed
  diagnostics: []
- case: c() coercion and an if expression join are clean
  diagnostics: []
- case: a for loop accumulator is clean
  diagnostics: []
- case: vectorized arithmetic and which() are clean
  diagnostics: []
- case: a multi-line magrittr chain after library(magrittr)
  diagnostics: []
- case: a merge() result column takes arithmetic
  diagnostics: []
- case: a read.csv() column selection takes arithmetic
  diagnostics: []
- case: a gc() matrix column takes arithmetic
  diagnostics: []
- case: a one-index merge() subset takes arithmetic
  diagnostics: []
- case: a one-index subset of a plain list stays a list
  diagnostics:
    - code: RY040
      line: 99
      message: "cannot apply arithmetic op to `list` and `double`"
      severity: error
- case: "a data frame's character column still rejects arithmetic"
  diagnostics:
    - code: RY040
      line: 106
      message: "cannot apply arithmetic op to `character` and `double`"
      severity: error
- case: a local data or load function is not the utils or base loader
  diagnostics: []
- case: data still binds the dataset it loads
  diagnostics:
    - code: RY061
      line: 140
      message: "$ operator is invalid for atomic vectors of mode `character`"
      severity: error
- case: only a union with a function member shadows the data loader
  diagnostics: []
- case: a data parameter with a non-function default shadows the loader
  diagnostics: []
- case: covr traces a function with a quoted exit call
  diagnostics: []
- case: an unbound helper in a trace() exit call still reports
  diagnostics:
    - code: RY010
      line: 184
      message: "variable `instrument_missing` is not bound in this scope"
      severity: warning
- case: covr calls its registered native routines by symbol
  diagnostics: []
- case: an unbound .Call() data argument still reports
  diagnostics:
    - code: RY010
      line: 206
      message: "variable `new_value` is not bound in this scope"
      severity: warning
- case: covr evaluates code under withr and matches gcov output with rex
  diagnostics: []
- case: "code run under withr::with_envvar() is still checked"
  diagnostics:
    - code: RY040
      line: 242
      message: "cannot apply arithmetic op to `double` and `character`"
      severity: error
